        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 24 at 5:22PM PDT until September 25 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS Pendleton OR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Southwest winds 20 to 35 mph with gusts of 40 to 55 mph
expected.

* WHERE...Lower Columbia Basin of Washington and Foothills of the
Blue Mountains of Washington.

* WHEN...From 11 AM to 11 PM PDT Friday.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Strongest winds are expected in the afternoon
and early evening.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.

Secure outdoor objects.

Patchy blowing dust may reduce visibility. Use caution if traveling
and be ready for a sudden drop in visibility if you encounter blowing
dust.</instruction>
